  "helpPairTwoWaysShort": "A request to a contact, or your code.",
  "@helpPairTwoWaysShort": {
    "description": "Help topic lede."
  },
  "helpPairTwoWaysP1": "**Pair with a contact.** On a contact you have paid or been paid by over Epicbox, Pair sends a request to that address. Their wallet shows it when it is open; one tap answers. Both wallets end Verified without a words check: the request and the answer each prove the address already in the other’s Contacts.",
  "@helpPairTwoWaysP1": {
    "description": "Help: Way 1."
  },
  "helpPairTwoWaysP2": "**Pair by code.** Contacts › Pair shows your code, good for 7 days. The other wallet scans it or opens the link; both finish over Epicbox and then compare the four words. With Epicbox off on either side, the same screen carries the answer and the finish code by hand: Share and Paste.",
  "@helpPairTwoWaysP2": {
    "description": "Help: Way 2."
  },
  "helpPairTwoWaysP3": "A request is sent only to a wallet that has shown it runs BT Wallet: a marked payment between the two addresses within the last 30 days. For anyone else, Pair shows your code.",
  "@helpPairTwoWaysP3": {
    "description": "Help: when a request can be sent."
  },
  "helpPairWhyTitle2": "Why check the words",
  "@helpPairWhyTitle2": {
    "description": "Help topic title (words check)."
  },
  "helpPairWhyShort2": "Compare them in person, by voice or video.",
  "@helpPairWhyShort2": {
    "description": "Help topic lede."
  },
  "helpPairWhyP1b": "After pairing by code both wallets show the same four pictures and names. Compare them with the other person in person, by voice or on a video call, never in the chat the code came through: whoever could change the code on the way could also change what that chat shows.",
  "@helpPairWhyP1b": {
    "description": "Help: how to compare."
  },
  "helpPairWhyP2b": "**They match** marks the contact Verified; the other wallet learns of it and shows “confirmed too”. **They do not match** ends the pairing on both sides and nothing sent through it is finished. A mistaken No ends it too: pair again with a fresh code.",
  "@helpPairWhyP2b": {
    "description": "Help: what the two answers do."
  },
  "helpPairWhyP3b": "Verified means the wallet behind the address in your Contacts. After a request between two contacts it is set without words, because the request and the answer each proved that address.",
  "@helpPairWhyP3b": {
    "description": "Help: what Verified means."
  },
  "helpPairWhyP4b": "“Proven” means a payment marked by both wallets has passed between the two Epicbox addresses within 30 days. A contact answered by another wallet app since then is not proven until the next marked payment.",
  "@helpPairWhyP4b": {
    "description": "Help: what proven means."
  },
  "pairStandingFootnote": "Good for 7 days. A new invite appears when this one is used.",
  "@pairStandingFootnote": {
    "description": "Pair screen footnote under the invite (desktop)."
  },
